<!-- ABSTRACT -->
<h1>ABSTRACT</h1>
<p>This project focuses on the design and development of a Network Usage Monitoring System to improve the efficiency of managing network operations. Many small organizations rely on semi-automated record keeping and manual router checks, which often leads to bandwidth inaccuracies and difficulty in tracking device performance. The developed system provides a digital platform that allows the network administrator to manage device inventory, record usage metrics, and generate reports. The system was developed using PHP with HTML, CSS, and JavaScript for the interface and MySQL for the database. The system improves accuracy, enhances network control, and helps the administrator make better decisions through organized and real-time information management.</p>

<div class="page-break"></div>

<!-- DEFINITION OF KEY TERMS -->
<h1>DEFINITION OF KEY TERMS</h1>
<p><strong>Network Usage Monitoring System</strong> - A computerized system used to track, manage, and control network devices and bandwidth utilization, including adding, updating, and monitoring available hardware.</p>
<p><strong>Database</strong> - An organized collection of data stored electronically that allows easy access, management, and updating of information such as device records and metric transactions.</p>
<p><strong>User Authentication</strong> - A security process that verifies the identity of a user by checking login credentials such as a username and password before granting access to the system.</p>
<p><strong>Dashboard</strong> - A graphical user interface that displays key information such as total devices, threshold alerts, and daily traffic to help the user monitor system performance.</p>
<p><strong>Metric Log</strong> - A record that keeps track of all network readings made in the system, including device name, download, upload, date, and latency.</p>
<p><strong>Threshold Alert</strong> - A system notification that warns the user when the bandwidth consumption of a particular device exceeds a predefined limit.</p>
<p><strong>Entity Relationship Diagram (ERD)</strong> - A visual representation that shows how different data entities such as users, devices, metrics, and alerts are related within a database.</p>
<p><strong>Data Flow Diagram (DFD)</strong> - A diagram that illustrates how data moves through the system and how it is processed between different components.</p>
<p><strong>PHP PDO Framework</strong> - A robust server-side scripting environment in PHP used to build the backend logic and secure database access for the network monitoring system.</p>
<p><strong>Deployment</strong> - The process of making the system available for use by hosting it on a server so users can access it through a local network or the internet.</p>

