<h1>CHAPTER TWO: DESIGN AND MODELING</h1>

<h2>Introduction to Modelling</h2>
<p>This chapter presents the system designs and models developed to visualize the proposed network usage monitoring system before the actual implementation began. The diagrams and models illustrate how the system would function, how users would interact with it and how data would flow within the system. Modeling the system prior to development helped to clarify requirements, identify potential challenges early and ensure that all system components are well organized. This approach reduces development errors, improves planning and provides a clear blueprint that guides the implementation process, resulting in an efficient, reliable and a well-structured system.</p>

