<h1>CHAPTER THREE: SYSTEM IMPLEMENTATION</h1>

<h2>Introduction</h2>
<p>This chapter focuses on the implementation of the system, detailing the journey from development to deployment. It begins with the development process, explaining how the design specifications and requirements were transformed into a working application using suitable programming tools, frameworks, and technologies. The chapter then discusses the testing phase, highlighting the methods employed to identify and correct errors, ensure system reliability, and confirm that all functionalities meet user requirements. Finally, it covers the deployment process, describing how the system was prepared for actual use, including installation, configuration, and user accessibility considerations. Throughout the chapter, challenges encountered during each stage are explained along with the solutions applied, providing insight into the practical aspects of system implementation.</p>

<h2>User Interface Development</h2>

<h3>Login Page Development</h3>
<p>The login form allows users to securely access the Network Usage Monitoring System by entering a valid username and password. It captures input data, validates user credentials, and authenticates access. Upon successful login, users are granted entry to the system, while incorrect details prompt error messages, ensuring secure and controlled system access.</p>

